{"schema_version":1,"stream":"steps","idempotency_key":"step:run_f7bdb11faf8d:reviewer:commit:0:0","created_at":"2026-10-19 22:36:06","provenance":"recorded","origin":{"recorder":{"installation_id":"eca1b52d-1c4f-4337-9c73-d8c035d3b08c"},"performer":{"kind":"agent","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude-code"}},"payload":{"step_name":"reviewer:commit","phase":"0","iteration":0,"result_json":{"readiness":"ready_with_corrections","items":[{"id":"P2.1","title":"Repeated-recovery attribution rule is ambiguous about cumulative invalidation sets","action":"auto_fix","reason":"Every historical recovery writer (81eddb4, a15d7b9, implementation-recovery.ts:412-418) computes invalidatedContextIds/invalidatedObservationIds cumulatively over all prior affected-phase evidence. The verification record frames the check per between-recovery segment and says an extra id fails closed, so one reading fails closed on valid repeated same-frontier recoveries.","priority":"P2","scopeClass":"implementation_defect","effortDelta":0,"architectureDelta":0,"failure":"The Phase 1 fold, implemented from the segment-scoped wording, rejects a second recovery at the same frontier because its set repeats ids already invalidated by the first recovery. A valid legacy run then reports fail-closed diagnostics.","lowestCostCorrection":"Edit the Budget-stream evidence bullet in phase-0-verification.md to state cumulative prefix equality, matching implementation-recovery.ts:412-418.","planWorkItemIds":["W1"],"boundaryChanges":[],"mechanicalExplanation":"Restate the rule as exact equality with the cumulative set the recovery writer computes: in the budget prefix before recovery R, all binding contexts and all observations on phases at or after R frontier, ordered by the predecessor authorized bytes. Extra means an id outside that set."}],"summary":"Phase 0 is a verification-only phase with no product code. The commit records the integrated commit, reader inventory, gate identity ruling, legacy codec and keys, causal attribution algorithm, upgrade discovery, mutation boundary and codec fit. The claims checked against the 4af6e20 tree hold, and the recovery regression tests pass. One P2 wording correction: the repeated-recovery attribution rule must be stated as cumulative prefix equality so the Phase 1 fold does not fail closed on valid repeated same-frontier recoveries."},"head_commit":"e66fe176f7fcfffeaa1d32fee8eb3d210c738a9e","patch_id":null,"diff_summary":{"files_changed":0,"insertions":0,"deletions":0},"duration_ms":178949,"tokens_in":60,"tokens_out":18538,"cost_usd":1.4984429999999997,"model":"claude-opus-5-5"}}
